data: {"type":"response.function_call_arguments.done","sequence_number":429,"item_id":"fc_04de6b92baab60ea016adb43caf3d081918720b2ac00277086","output_index":1,"arguments":"{\"obstacle_json\":\"{\\\"status\\\":\\\"TASK_INCOMPLETE\\\",\\\"location\\\":\\\"same-stage candidate 11, R002 ambient Lebesgue premise and all remaining proof repairs\\\",\\\"explanation\\\":\\\"Continued from candidate 6 without resetting. Registered additional real Mathlib sources M013 (finite-coordinate volume product), M014 (real interval volume), and M016 (compact sets are bounded), wired them as direct R002 inputs, and the latest candidate structurally checks. These sources are ingredients, not yet the complete proof that the Euclidean Lebesgue measure is finite on every compact; R002 still must actually derive that property and clarify the Borel/Lebesgue ambient. R004 has not yet been rewritten using M011/N001 and its actual derivative/integrability hypotheses. Thus no complete artifact is submitted; this remains unfinished mathematical expansion, not a substantive gap.\\\",\\\"basis\\\":\\\"check_draft on base_candidate 10 yielded candidate 11 with STRUCTURE-PASSED only. Successful probes M013 volume_pi_pi, M014 Real.volume_Icc, M016 IsCompact.isBounded; official M016 source context inspected. Prior candidate 6 remains ancestor in this same-stage edit chain.\\\",\\\"partial_progress\\\":\\\"Candidate 11 adds M016, M013, M014 and direct R002 input/application records; candidate 6 already contained corrected full_target, M015 integral_zero used in R001, expanded N001 quantifiers, and R003's C∪{0} nonempty-support treatment. Current graph has 5 inferences and passes structural validation, but sources/applications/prose have not undergone a new mathematical review. Remaining: prove finite measure for every compact K from coordinate boundedness and box-volume formula with complete quantifiers/declarations, settle Euclidean Borel/Lebesgue ambient structures faithfully, directly use N001 in R00